.DS_STORE
.DS_Store
node_modules
bin/
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.*.example

*.bun-build
.labkit

# This is a Bun project — `bun.lock` is the lockfile. A tracked
# `package-lock.json` was removed after the two disagreed about drizzle-kit
# (0.30.6 vs 0.18.1) with nothing reading the npm one. Ignored so an
# accidental `npm install` cannot resurrect a second source of truth.
package-lock.json

.idea

# Claude Code, shared vs local.
#
# `.claude/settings.json` (the wrap Stop/SessionStart wiring) and
# `.claude/skills/` are checked in deliberately — a clone or a new worktree
# needs both for the hook to run at all.
#
# What stays out is machine- or session-local:
.claude/settings.local.json
# hookify rules — enforcement, not record. Each encodes an incident that already
# has a durable home in docs/TASKS.md or docs/session-log/; these files only
# make the machine nag about it. `.local` is hookify's own convention for
# machine-scoped rules.
.claude/hookify.*.local.md
# One file per session, keyed by a session UUID, holding three lines derived
# from git. Meaningless in another checkout, rewritten constantly by concurrent
# sessions, and swept on a timer — a tracked copy would conflict, go stale, and
# hand a new worktree some other session's pinned baseline.
.claude/.wrap-state/

# Terraform. `*.tfvars` holds the billing account id; state holds everything
# else about the project, including service-account emails and, in some
# providers, secrets. `.terraform/` is a provider cache the size of a binary.
infra/**/*.tfvars
infra/**/.terraform/
infra/**/*.tfstate
infra/**/*.tfstate.*

# `.terraform.lock.hcl` is deliberately NOT ignored: it pins provider versions
# and belongs in the repo for the same reason `bun.lock` does.
